# 1. Equivalence Partitioning (EP) – Phone Number Field

**Requirement:** The phone number must contain exactly **10 digits**. Letters and special characters are not allowed.

Using EP, we divide the input into valid and invalid groups.

| Partition     | Input Condition             | Example       | Expected Result |
| ------------- | --------------------------- | ------------- | --------------- |
| **Valid**     | Exactly 10 digits           | `9876543210`  | Accepted        |
| **Invalid 1** | Less than 10 digits         | `987654321`   | Rejected        |
| **Invalid 2** | More than 10 digits         | `98765432101` | Rejected        |
| **Invalid 3** | Contains letters            | `98765AB210`  | Rejected        |
| **Invalid 4** | Contains special characters | `98765@3210`  | Rejected        |
| **Invalid 5** | Blank input                 | Empty         | Rejected        |

So, instead of testing every possible phone number, we test one or more representative values from each partition.

