# 2. Boundary Value Analysis (BVA) – Password Field

**Requirement:** Password length must be between **8 and 16 characters**.

For BVA, we mainly check values around the boundaries.

| Test Case  | Password Length | Example               | Expected Result |
| ---------- | --------------: | --------------------- | --------------- |
| **TC-P01** |               7 | `Abc1234`             | ❌ Rejected      |
| **TC-P02** |               8 | `Abc12345`            | ✅ Accepted      |
| **TC-P03** |               9 | `Abc123456`           | ✅ Accepted      |
| **TC-P04** |              15 | 15-character password | ✅ Accepted      |
| **TC-P05** |              16 | 16-character password | ✅ Accepted      |
| **TC-P06** |              17 | 17-character password | ❌ Rejected      |

**Conclusion:** The accepted boundary is **8–16 characters**. Values 7 and 17 should be rejected.

