# 3. Equivalence Partitioning – Instagram Caption

**Requirement:** Caption can contain a maximum of **2200 characters**.

We can divide the input into these partitions:

| Partition |           Character Range | Valid/Invalid |
| --------- | ------------------------: | ------------- |
| **P1**    |              0 characters | Valid         |
| **P2**    |         1–2200 characters | Valid         |
| **P3**    | More than 2200 characters | Invalid       |

### Test Cases

| Test Case ID | Partition               | Test Data       | Expected Result                                                        |
| ------------ | ----------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **TC-C01**   | P1 – Empty              | 0 characters    | Caption should be accepted if captions are optional.                   |
| **TC-C02**   | P2 – Normal             | 50 characters   | Caption should be accepted.                                            |
| **TC-C03**   | P2 – Near maximum       | 2200 characters | Caption should be accepted.                                            |
| **TC-C04**   | P3 – Over limit         | 2201 characters | Caption should be rejected or extra characters should not be accepted. |
| **TC-C05**   | P3 – Clearly over limit | 2500 characters | Caption should be rejected or restricted to the allowed limit.         |
| **TC-C06**   | P3 – Large input        | 3000 characters | Application should handle it properly without crashing.                |
| **TC-C07**   | P2 – Small input        | 1 character     | Caption should be accepted.                                            |
| **TC-C08**   | P2 – Medium input       | 1000 characters | Caption should be accepted.                                            |
| **TC-C09**   | P2 – Maximum            | 2199 characters | Caption should be accepted.                                            |

So the important EP idea is that **0–2200 is the valid class**, while **anything above 2200 is an invalid class**.

